# Change: C-Am and Am-Dm (repertoire plan: st-change-c-am-am-dm). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half (home C): C (x32010) with Am (x02210); fingers 1 and 2 stay down, only
# finger 3 moves (string 5 fret 3 to string 3 fret 2). Second half (home Am): Am with Dm (xx0231);
# the A on string 3, fret 2 stays but changes finger (3 in Am, 2 in Dm). Strum C and Am on
# strings 5 to 1, Dm on strings 4 to 1. Keep the metronome on: the new chord lands on the beat
# even if the strum before it catches open strings. The last Am is held for two beats to close.
# The teacher plays an original tune over your chords, a chord tone on every strong beat; the
# first half ends on C, the second on A (F-E-D falling to A over Dm and Am).
title: Change: C-Am and Am-Dm
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, anchor fingers
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: C

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[C and Am]
| ^"One strum a bar, from string 5" "C=x32010" w D | D | ^"Two strums a bar" "Am=x02210" h D D | "C=x32010" D D |
| ^"Four strums a bar" "Am=x02210" q D D D D | "C=x32010" D D D D | ^"Change every two beats" "Am=x02210" D D "C=x32010" D D | "Am=x02210" D D "C=x32010" D D ||
key: Am
[Am and Dm]
| ^"Am to Dm: the A stays, the finger changes" "Am=x02210" w D | D | ^"Dm on strings 4-1" "Dm=xx0231" h D D | "Am=x02210" D D |
| "Dm=xx0231" q D D D D | "Am=x02210" D D D D | "Dm=xx0231" D D "Am=x02210" D D | "Dm=xx0231" D D "Am=x02210" h D ||

track: Teacher
role: lead
[C and Am]
| q 2:1 1:0 1:3 1:0 | h 2:1 3:0 | h 3:2 q 2:1 1:0 | h 1:3 1:0 |
| q 1:0 2:3 2:1 2:0 | h 2:1 1:0 | h 2:1 1:3 | h 1:0 2:1 ||
[Am and Dm]
| q 3:2 2:1 1:0 2:1 | h 3:2 1:0 | h 2:3 1:1 | w 1:0 |
| q 1:1 1:0 2:3 3:2 | h 2:1 1:0 | h 1:1 1:0 | h 2:3 3:2 ||
